    kg:textSpan "many peers, the remaining ones will face an increased processing load, which will inevitably form a bottleneck. Stochastic wiring. To better utilize heterogeneous devices and recover from faults, we dynamically wire each input through each stage and pick devices in proportion to their training throughput. To achieve this, SWARM peers run trainer processes that route training data through the stages of SWARM, balancing the load between peers. For each pipeline stage, trainers discover which peers" .

