    kg:textSpan "is flatter than in the case of the other two schemes. The convergence trajectories of different distributed optimizers can be found in Appendix A. Consider the problem of minimizing a loss function F with respect to model parameters x over a large data set D . In a parallel computing environment with M workers ( x 1 , x 2 , ..., x M ), this optimization problem can be written as: min x F ( x ; D ) = M X m =1 E D m f ( x m ; ) + min x 1 ,...,x M where D is partitioned and sent to m workers and, D" .

