    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2406_10707v1_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "incur higher checkpointing overhead because the entire state of the application (including non-critical data structures) is captured and flushed to disk. Application-level checkpointrestart runtimes such as VELOC [ 20 22 , 26 ] and FTI [ 3 , 28 ] require the application to mark critical data structures necessary to restart application from failures for both CPU-only and hybrid CPU-GPU applications. Canary [ 2 ] supports containerized checkpointing. However, none of these runtimes exploit the imm" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2406_10707v1_rag__chunk_009> a kg:Chunk ;
