    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2406_10707v1_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "each of these shards needs to be flushed to persistent storage, typically as a separate file, as illustrated in Figure 2(c). In this case, conventional asynchronous multi-level approaches would serialize the checkpointing of the shards. For example, if we consider three shards in a checkpoint, two of which correspond to layers 1 and 2 and the third corresponds to the optimizer state shard, then only the flushing of the optimizer state shard will overlap with the next iteration (forward pass, bac" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2406_10707v1_rag__chunk_013> a kg:Chunk ;
