    kg:textSpan "host memory) by storing their memory pointers and sizes; (2) create a header by computing the file offsets for each tensor/object marked for asynchronous transfer in step (1); and (3) enqueue asynchronous device-to-host transfer (if required) and host-to-disk writes of headers, tensors and large objects (obtained in step-1). DeepSpeed: This is the default checkpointing approach used in the DeepSpeed [ 34 ] LLM training runtime using PyTorchs default torch.save() approach. This approach blocks th" .

