    kg:textSpan "face when supporting these techniques. 2.1 Distributed Training Large Models Training large models in a distributed manner reduces the memory requirements per device and accelerates the computation throughputs. Fully Sharded Data Parallel (FSDP) Zhao et al. ( 2023 ) is one of the most fundamental forms of data parallelism in distributed training. It shards model parameters, gradients, and optimizer states across multiple devices. During training, it gathers the needed parameters for computation " .

