    kg:textSpan "b i X N X N X = 1 B ) 1 N b i B i =1 where ij is the gradient on the j -th data input of GPU i . Cephalo is built on top of FSDP ( Zhao et al. , 2023 ), which divides the training state and computation evenly across each GPU. To balance compute, Cephalo assigns a batch size to each GPU proportional to its compute speed. To balance memory utilization, Cephalo partitions the training state and decides on configurations for gradient accumulation, activation checkpointing, and activation offloading " .

