    kg:docId "2412.01523_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2412_01523_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "inefficiency is pronounced. Therefore, we propose to adapting appropriate parallelism strategies, crafting heterogeneous parallelism groups to match the heterogeneous workloads caused by varied-length sequences. Specifically, we wish to form small groups for short sequences to improve efficiency, while retaining large groups for long sequences to avoid out-of-memory errors. Additionally, we need to properly control the assignment of sequences to balance the execution time among all parallelism g" .

