    kg:textSpan "of our modeling in 5.3 . NCCL supports two common algorithms for all-reduce : ring-based [ 9 ] and tree-based [ 3 ]. Figure 7 illustrates how they work. Other CC kernels use ring-based algorithm only. T Ring all gather = + ( N 1 ) , (2) T Ring reduce scatter = + ( N 1 )+ ( N 1 ) + tensor _ size , (3) T Ring all reduce = + ( N 1 )+ 2 ( N 1 ) + tensor _ size , (4) T Tree all reduce = + ( 1 )+ 2 ( K 1 ) + 2 log 2 ( M )+ tensor _ size . (5) Here N is the total number of devices, M number of nodes (s" .

