    kg:textSpan "for pipeline parallelism to work efficiently we have to ensure that each computation is scheduled at the right pipeline execution unit where the data are pinned while at the same time minimizing communication across actors. We assume that the loop schedule maps backward computations to the same actor of the corresponding forward computation. For example if weights W 1 and W 2 are placed on a specific actor then all the computation corresponding to the backward computation for the gradients of W " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2412_21124_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
