    kg:textSpan "of the data. The gradients calculated by each GPU are then averaged and synchronized across all GPUs to ensure consistent model updates. This method is particularly effective in leveraging the computational power of multiple GPUs to handle large datasets and improve training speed. To address these challenges, the training of large-scale Transformer models necessitates the use of distributed training across multiple GPUs ( Narayanan et al. , 2021b ; Li et al. , 2020 ; Narayanan et al. , 2019 ). " .

