    kg:textSpan "of the communicated tensors, while computation cost is measured by the number of floating-point operations required by each operator. In practice, there is a substantial gap between the cost estimated by the symbolic model and the actual performance produced during execution. Consider data and tensor parallelism for the transformer layer in Fig.1(b). Given a hidden_size of 5120, seq_len of 1024, and batch_size of 16, Alpa [ 51 ] estimates the cost of each parallelism plan by theoretically analyz" .

