    kg:textSpan "average edges. The construction involves three steps: (1) Sorting the contraction operators based on topological depth, which requires ( + + log ) time. (2) Constructing each ParallelBlock using DFS traversal, taking ( + ) as each operator and edge is visited at most once, to construct the affine transformation and compose it with previous accumulated dependency; (3) For ParallelBlocks, checking edges (intermediate tensors) to find potential cheaper resharding points, with ( ) complexity. Overal" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2504_00598_rag__chunk_015> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2504.00598_rag::chunk_015" ;
    kg:docId "2504.00598_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2504_00598_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "addition, the compilation time for parallel programs can also be substantial, especially when the computation graph is long but training workload is light-weight. To further mitigate the overhead, CFP introduces two optimizations: First, it enforces a dynamic profiling time budget, which is continuously updated based on the fastest observed parallelism plans, aggressively trimming the profiling of inefficient or stalled executions. Second, it parallelizes the compilation of different programs an" .

