    kg:textSpan "a novel observation: to our best knowledge, we are the first to identify that important gradients in LLM fine-tuning exhibit strong spatial and temporal locality. Specifically, we find that a small subset of input dimensions (i.e., channels) consistently carries highmagnitude gradients across training steps. By tracking and reusing this compact set of important channels, ZenFlow enables efficient, scalable importance-aware training without expensive global synchronization. This paper makes the f" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2505_12242_rag__chunk_005> a kg:Chunk ;
