    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2505_12242_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "It has been widely observed that the gradients of different parameters have different importance in deep neural network (DNN) training [ 3 , 13 , 25 , 42 ]. For example, Fig. 4 shows that top 1% of gradients account for 90% of the gradient norm. However, the current offloading techniques overlook this difference in gradients, treating them equally and offloading all of them to the CPU regardless of their impacts. This uniform treatment introduces unnecessary inefficiencies. Important gradient up" .

