    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2505_12242_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "is to overlap CPU updates with GPU computation using a strawman method such as layer-wise scheduling (Fig. 2(b)). In this strategy, each layers gradients are offloaded and updated sequentially during the backward pass, allowing the CPU to begin updating earlier layers while the GPU continues computing later ones. This pipelined execution enables partial overlap between CPU-side parameter updates and the GPU-side backward computation. For example, as soon as the gradient for layer is computed, it" .

