    kg:textSpan "learning has not yet been vetted for production use largely due to a lack of stability caused by the many fluctuations and vast differences in losses and/or accuracy of local training results across accelerators when scaling up. The previous studies ( Li et al. , 2020 ) believe that, these fluctuations and differences may be deleterious to model convergence, especially when scaling up accelerators, datasets, and/or models. Our proposals . For decentralized learning, to bridge the gap between its" .

