    kg:textSpan "Take the last bucket as an example. In order for the last buckets optimizer state to be executed on CPU, it requires a three-stage process: (i) gradient swap-out from GPU to CPU, (ii) execution of the Adam optimization algorithm on CPU, and (iii) swapin the updated parameters back to the GPU. Since the first parameter in the forward pass is updated by the last gradient created in the backward pass, all of the above processes cannot overlap with any computation on GPU because the GPU needs to wai" .

