    kg:textSpan "of diffusion models cannot be handled well by traditional pipelining methods. A diffusion model typically contains a trainable part with one or multiple backbone models (e.g., U-Net) ( Rombach et al. , 2022 ), and a nontrainable part with frozen text and image encoders, and they are usually trained with special techniques such as selfconditioning ( Chen et al. , 2022 ), which involves an additional forward computation pass on the backbone. Pipeline training involves only the trainable part, whil" .

