    kg:textSpan "presented in Figure 9 , which shows the memory usage and TFLOPs achieved by each schedule. The 1F1B schedule has the lowest memory usage due to its prioritization of the backward pass, but it achieves the lowest TFLOPs due to exposed P2P communications. In contrast, the all-forward-all-backward schedule achieves the highest TFLOPs by processing more micro-batches to hide exposed P2Ps, but it results in the highest memory usage. Flexible PP strikes a balance between memory usage and training thro" .

