    kg:docId "Y2I0Fy4sm7_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/Y2I0Fy4sm7_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "Data Parallelism (FSDP) shards both model parameters and input data across multiple GPUs[ 19 ]. These techniques usually gather full parameters only when needed and reduce-scatter the newly computed gradients across peers, significantly alleviating memory pressure on the accelerators while introducing considerable communication overhead. While distribution frameworks still require substantial hardware, offloading approaches address memory shortages in a different way. Work including ZeRO-Offload" .

