    kg:docId "ZO5cn4IfaN_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/ZO5cn4IfaN_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "integrations. In particular, with respect to ZeRO-3, which entails more sophisticated communication during both forward and backward passes, we had considered its compatibility with CO2. Given CO2s local-updating behavior in the inner loop, continuous gradient synchronization is deemed unnecessary at each step. As a result, communication operations for CO2 with ZeRO-3 involve only two all-gather collective communication primitives at the beginning of the forward and backward passes, respectively" .

