    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/swzhang-eurosys24_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "and uneven interconnect bandwidth in many clusters. Efficient exploitation of available heterogeneous resources for DNN training has piqued significant interest from AI practitioners [ 16 , 25 , 27 , 30 , 43 , 53 , 56 ]. A prevalent approach for making use of heterogeneous clusters is to distribute multiple training jobs onto different homogeneous subsets of the cluster [ 50 , 57 ]. However, this approach imposes a constraint on the maximum model size, as it is bound by the capacity of the subse" .

