    :hasEvidenceText "Data Parallelism : This technique ( Li et al. , 2020 ) distributes different data subsets across devices. While it shards the batch inputs and activations, each machine holds a complete copy of the models weights and gradients"^^xsd:string,
        "Data parallelism (DP) [ 25 , 50 ] shards the input data along the batch dimension"^^xsd:string,
        "Data parallelism . In DP, each GPU has a model replica and half of the input data samples."^^xsd:string,
        "Data parallelism and model parallelism are two mainstream parallel training solutions. The former distributes sample data across devices to increase the throughput"^^xsd:string,
        "Data parallelism is the most widely used technique to accelerate the training of deep learning models [ 16 ]. It creates replicas of the learning model on multiple workers"^^xsd:string,
        "Data parallelism plays a critical role in training models with large parameters and/or large training data on large-scale compute devices"^^xsd:string,
        "Data parallelism requires communication to aggregate gradients"^^xsd:string,
        "Data parallelism. Data parallelism approaches are widely used to scale up the distributed training for large input datasets. It refers to distributing the data samples across multiple workers"^^xsd:string,
        "For data parallelism , each GPU device possesses a complete replica of the model, while the input dataset is partitioned among these GPU devices."^^xsd:string,
        "In this case, data parallelism"^^xsd:string,
        "It creates replicas of the learning model on multiple workers, each of which is placed on a different device and/or compute node"^^xsd:string,
        "Pytorch FSDP training [ 38 ] supports only data parallelism and is less efficient than hybrid parallel strategies."^^xsd:string,
        "The global input batch is divided into multiple minibatches for each training step, so each worker performs forward and backward computations with a different minibatch."^^xsd:string,
        "When training data parallel models, which is the standard for distributed training, then all cores are allocated to the data-parallel dimension"^^xsd:string,
        "a combination of pipeline parallelism size 4 with data parallelism size 2."^^xsd:string,
        "a hybrid (2-way DP, 2-MP) approach performs better than both MP-only and DP-only"^^xsd:string,
        "adapt data parallelism by adding/removing model replicas to/from GPU worker"^^xsd:string,
        "algorithm that combines data, tensor, and expert parallelism to enable the training of MoE models."^^xsd:string,
        "computations in distributed environments, such as data and model parallelization"^^xsd:string,
        "parallelism for each layer is either data parallelism or model parallelism"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        :hybrid_parallelism,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "DataParallelism"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A standard distributed training approach where cores are allocated to the data-parallel dimension, requiring no communication until the forward and backward passes are finished."^^xsd:string ;
