    :hasEvidenceText "1- D tensor parallelism to partition the first parameter matrix along its column, and the second parameter matrix along its row."^^xsd:string,
        "Two sub-paradigms within model parallelism are pipeline parallelism and tensor parallelism"^^xsd:string,
        "Two sub-paradigms within model parallelism are pipeline parallelism and tensor parallelism ."^^xsd:string,
        "Under model parallelism, each task/device has only a portion of parameters."^^xsd:string,
        "Under model parallelism, each task/device has only a portion of parameters. That reduces the storage burden"^^xsd:string,
        "employ a maximum TP degree, typically set at 8, to reduce the activation memory per device."^^xsd:string,
        "tensor parallelism to partition the first parameter matrix along its column, and the second parameter matrix along its row."^^xsd:string,
        "tensor parallelism where tensors are fully involved in computations"^^xsd:string,
        "tensor parallelism, it is confined to the same node and communicates via PCI-E or NVLink interfaces."^^xsd:string ;
