    kg:textSpan "of node-local GPUs in order to take advantage of fast 600 GB/s NVLinks to mitigate communication overheads. The combination of data parallelism, pipeline parallelism, and tensor parallelism is often called 3D parallelism . 2 BACKGROUND 2.1 Data Parallelism Data parallelism is the most widely used technique to accelerate the training of deep learning models [ 16 ]. It creates replicas of the learning model on multiple workers, each of which is placed on a different device and/or compute node, as " .

