    kg:textSpan "Offloading When it comes to offloading LLM training, a key issue is to determine what model states to offload from GPU to CPU. While CPUs offer large memory capacity, transferring model states to and from CPU memory still incurs time delays. Given that both the forward propagation and backward propagation of LLM training have a computation complexity of ( ) and the optimizer state update has a complexity of ( ) , where is the batch size, state-of-the-art offloading systems often offload optimize" .

