    kg:textSpan "Yadan et al. ( Yadan et al. , 2013 ) show that a hybrid (2-way DP, 2-MP) approach performs better than both MP-only and DP-only when training AlexNet on a 4-GPU system, but do not discuss the cause of the results or evaluate this effect across different GPU counts. Dean et al. ( Dean et al. , 2012 ) used hybrid parallelism to train models which would not t in a single GPUs memory. Therefore, in each data parallel worker, the model replica is model parallelized across multiple devices. However wi" .

