    kg:textSpan "Figure 2 , 1F1B initiates with a warm-up phase. In this phase, workers conduct varying numbers of forward passes, with each stage typically performing one more forward pass than its immediately subsequent stage. Following the warm-up phase, each worker transits to a steady state where they alternately execute one forward pass and one backward pass, ensuring an even workload distribution among stages. In the final phase, each worker processes the backward passes for the outstanding in-flight micr" .

