    kg:textSpan "(Jain et al. 2020; Li and Hoefler 2021; Zhang et al. 2023), each device stores multiple pipeline stages in different directions, which decreases bubble size and achieves a more balanced activation memory consumption. On the other hand, interleaved approaches (Narayanan et al. 2021b; Lamy-Poirier 2023; Liu et al. 2023) assign multiple smaller and nonconsecutive stages to each device, which makes each bubble size smaller accordingly. Despite the promising results, the latest synchronous approaches" .

