    kg:textSpan "( Luo et al. , 2022 ) and Chimera ( Li & Hoefler , 2021 ), such approaches cannot fundamentally eliminate pipeline bubbles, as they only manipulate the trainable part of the model and do not take the non-trainable part into consideration. Self-conditioning ( Chen et al. , 2022 ) has become a very popular technique for training diffusion models ( Rombach et al. , 2022 ; Saharia et al. , 2022 ; Yuan et al. , 2022 ), which improves the sampling quality by introducing an additional forward computati" .

