    kg:textSpan "2020) is a memory-efficient pipeline approach that first schedules micro-batches among two model replicas. Since GEMS is mainly designed for small batch sizes and executes at most two micro-batches simultaneously, its bubble ratio is much higher than that of the other approaches. Chimera (Li and Hoefler 2021) implements two pipelines in opposite directions simultaneously (named down and up pipeline, respectively), and the pipeline utilization can be better than that of vanilla pipeline paralleli" .

