    kg:docId "2410.12707_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2410_12707_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "(b) ResNet101 with Tiny-ImageNet. (c) GPT2-XL with Wikitext-2. Figure 8. Training loss with different model architectures and datasets. Dense means training without compression. All compression ratio is set as 100. which equally assigns the same number of user-defined modules on computing nodes; 2) equal computation costs, which firstly partitions user-defined modules with load balance and assign each computing node with on partition. Performance metrics. We use the averaged time costs as the la" .

